{
  "dom_id": "step-q335992",
  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(X=2).$\n\n| $x$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(x)$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.35$ | $0.60$ | $0.85$ | $1.00$ |\n\n$P(X=2)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(2) & =P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =P(X\\in {-1,0,1,2}) \\\\  & =P(X=-1)+P(X=0)+P(X=1)+P(X=2) \\\\  & =P(X\\in {-1,0,1})+P(X=2) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 1)+P(X=2) \\\\  & =F(1)+P(X=2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=2) & =F(2)-F(1) \\\\  & =0.60-0.35 \\\\  & =0.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
